membr:Hutta foaf:currentProject membr:Project_Hutta_2610271233 .

membr:Project_Hutta_2610271233_F2610271233 a rsrch:Finding ;
    RDFS:label """In dialects of German umlaut can be an obligatory element in a nominal plural construction, as well as an optional one. This means that depending on the specific regional variation, umlaut can serve as a singular element to form a nominal plural construction, it can be combined with a plural suffix to form a nominal plural construction, or the plural construction is only formed with a suffix. However,for 'Töchter' (dauchters) one element that forms plural is obligatory. \r
Aside from the number of elements that form the construction, there are a number of allomorphemic variants of each element, which are specific to the dialect or regional variation of German. """ ;
    rsrch:basedOn cx:deu_Toechter .

references:1495247b-1525-45be-9a55-c6fd421547bf evid:biblio "Dammel, Antje & Sebastian Kürschner. 2008. Complexity in nominal plural allomorphy: A contrastive survey of ten Germanic languages. In Language Complexity, 243–262. John Benjamins Publishing Company." .

references:4a94c6ad-4d31-47a7-887c-cf5a289137de evid:biblio "Audring, Jenny & Ray Jackendoff. 2025. Construction Morphology and Relational Morphology. InMirjam Fried & Kiki Nikiforidou (eds.), The Cambridge Handbook of Construction Grammar, 101–128. 1st edn. Cambridge University Press. https://doi.org/10.1017/9781009049139.005." .

references:4aa85e49-d3e2-448b-ac4b-9cb4dea93ede evid:biblio "Nübling, Damaris. 2001. Wechselflexion Luxemburgisch - Deutsch kontrastiv: “ech soen - du sees/si seet” vs. “ich sage, du sagst, sie sagt” : zum sekundären Ausbau eines präsentischen Wurzelvokalwechsels im Luxemburgischen. Sprachwissenschaft 26(4). 433–472." .

references:5526c23a-6142-48be-b061-244f9dcaee4a evid:biblio "Nübling, Damaris. 2013. Zwischen Konservierung, Eliminierung und Funktionalisierung: Der Umlaut in den germanischen Sprachen. Sprachwandelvergleich–Comparing Diachronies. Walter de Gruyter 550. 15." .

references:6e9b6c5e-ac96-4685-9654-2f060c6f397c evid:biblio "Ruan, Junyu. 2024. Predictability changes in morphologization: A case study of German Umlaut. The Ohio State University." .

references:c33e68a9-a0d8-4eb6-800f-eb3d17f0cd9f evid:biblio "Knooihuizen, Remco & Oscar Strik. 2014. Relative productivity potentials of Dutch verbal inflection patterns. Folia Linguistica 35(1). https://doi.org/10.1515/flih.2014.005." .

references:d7faff17-6877-487b-b9ab-7cdb3cb1b20b evid:biblio "Van De Weijer, Jeroen, Weiyun Wei, Yumeng Wang, Guangyuan Ren & Yunyun Ran. 2020. Words are constructions, too: A construction-based approach to English ablaut reduplication. Linguistics 58(6). 1701–1735. https://doi.org/10.1515/ling-2020-0169." .

